INT. COPYING ROOM - MELLOR AND STROUD, LIVERPOOL - DAWN

Gas still lit. Eight sloping desks, one occupied.

ADA MELLOR, twenty-six, copies. Steel nib, a good hand, no waste in it. At the foot of each finished sheet she puts two small letters in the corner, close in against the rule: a m.

She dusts the wet ink with sand from a brass caster and tips the sand back.

MR. STROUD, sixty, comes through with his coat still on.

STROUD
The Wakefield's papers before the tide.

ADA
They're begun.

STROUD
They're begun.

ADA
They're half done, Mr Stroud, and they were begun at five.

STROUD
Then don't tell me they're begun. Tell me they're half done. A clerk who understates is a clerk who is hiding the other half.

He goes. Ada looks at the door a moment, then dips.

INT. COPYING ROOM - MORNING

Ada copies the manifest of the barque WAKEFIELD. Her eye runs the column: iron rail, sheet lead, salt, deals.

She reaches the burthen and writes it: four hundred and ten tons.

She blots. Sands. Puts a m in the corner.

INT. STROUD'S ROOM - MORNING

Stroud reads the fair copy at the window. He takes up his own pen, and without turning round, writes across the sheet.

STROUD
Copy it again.

ADA
Sir.

STROUD
And burn the first.

He hands it back. She reads it going down the passage.

The burthen now says nine hundred and sixty tons.

INT. COUNTING HOUSE - DAY

CAPTAIN HARROW, fifty, the owner's agent, salt-cured, warming his hands at the fire he has not been offered.

HARROW
She sails Thursday.

STROUD
She sails Thursday.

HARROW
With what aboard her?

STROUD
With what's on the manifest, Captain.

HARROW
That's a fine answer. That's an answer you could put in a frame.

Ada crosses the room with a tray of ink and neither man stops speaking, because she is furniture.

HARROW (CONT'D)
And the crew?

STROUD
Signed on short. Nine where she wants fourteen.

HARROW
Nine.

STROUD
It's a short sea, Captain. It's a fortnight of water.

INT. COPYING ROOM - EVENING

Empty desks. Ada alone with a candle.

She goes to the waste basket under Stroud's sloping desk and takes out her first fair copy, creased in four. Four hundred and ten tons. Her initials in the corner.

She flattens it on the desk with the side of her hand.

For a long moment she does nothing at all.

Then she takes a fresh sheet, copies the true manifest a second time, sands it, puts a m in the corner, and folds it into a cover which she addresses in a hand not her own to the Liverpool Underwriters' Association, Exchange Buildings.

She writes the entry in the letter book, because a letter unentered is a letter stolen.

Then she puts on her coat and takes it to the post herself.

INT. COPYING ROOM - MORNING

Stroud stands at the letter book with one finger on the page.

STROUD
Underwriters' Association.

ADA
Yes, sir.

STROUD
On whose instruction.

ADA
I entered it, sir, as the book requires.

STROUD
That is not the question I asked and you have answered it very well.

He closes the book softly, which is worse than slamming it.

EXT. SALTHOUSE DOCK - DAY

Rain on black water. The Wakefield warping out, low in it, too low.

A BOY runs along the quay with a paper. Ada takes it, reads it, folds it small.

She stands watching the barque until the masts are behind the warehouses.

INT. STROUD'S ROOM - DAY

STROUD
Your keys.

Ada puts them on the desk. Three keys, a brass rule beside them.

STROUD (CONT'D)
The rule's the house's.

ADA
The rule was my father's. He had this desk before you had that one.

STROUD
Then take it and take yourself. There'll be no character written for you.

ADA
No, sir. I didn't suppose there would be.

She takes the rule.

INT. COUNTING HOUSE - DAY

Harrow at the fire. With him a young UNDERWRITERS' CLERK holding a folded sheet. Stroud comes in fast, and stops.

UNDERWRITERS' CLERK
Four hundred and ten tons, Mr Stroud. Sworn insurance nine hundred and sixty.

STROUD
There's a copy in this house that says otherwise.

HARROW
There's a copy in this house in your hand, Stroud. This one's got initials on it.

He turns the sheet so the corner shows. a m, small, hard in against the rule.

HARROW (CONT'D)
Whose are those?

Stroud does not answer. Through the glass, the copying room: eight desks, all empty.

EXT. MELLOR AND STROUD - STREET - DAY

Ada on the step in the rain, the brass rule under her arm, no character, no place, no wages owing paid.

The door opens behind her. She does not turn round.

She walks off down the wet street, and her hand, without asking her, makes two small letters against her thumb.
